@page "/docs"
@model OrbitAccess.Pages.DocsModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Docs — Orbit Access";
}
<section class="page-band">
    <div class="container">
        <article class="page-prose">
            <span class="badge-pill">Documentation</span>
            <h1 class="display-lg">Docs</h1>
            <p class="body-md">Everything this app does, how to run it, and how it works inside. Signed-in workflows use the GitHub REST API and the Notion API.</p>

            <h2 class="title-md">Quick start</h2>
            <ol class="steps-ol body-md">
                <li>Create an OAuth App at <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/settings/developers" target="_blank" rel="noopener">github.com/settings/developers</a>. Any homepage/callback URL works — the app accepts GitHub's reply on the root path.</li>
                <li>Put your credentials in the environment or appsettings (see Configuration below).</li>
                <li>Run <code>dotnet run</code> in <code>OrbitAccess/</code> and open <code>http://localhost:3000</code>.</li>
            </ol>

            <h2 class="title-md">Configuration</h2>
            <div class="doc-list">
                <div class="doc-row"><code class="doc-path">GITHUB_CLIENT_ID</code><span class="chip-method">Required</span><p class="body-md doc-desc">From your OAuth App at github.com/settings/developers.</p></div>
                <div class="doc-row"><code class="doc-path">GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET</code><span class="chip-method">Required</span><p class="body-md doc-desc">The matching client secret. Server-side only — never shipped to the browser.</p></div>
                <div class="doc-row"><code class="doc-path">NOTION_CLIENT_ID</code><span class="chip-method">For Notion</span><p class="body-md doc-desc">From a public integration at notion.so/my-integrations (OAuth &amp; Services tab).</p></div>
                <div class="doc-row"><code class="doc-path">NOTION_CLIENT_SECRET</code><span class="chip-method">For Notion</span><p class="body-md doc-desc">The matching integration secret.</p></div>
                <div class="doc-row"><code class="doc-path">NOTION_REDIRECT_URI</code><span class="chip-method">Optional</span><p class="body-md doc-desc">Defaults to http://localhost:3000/notion/callback. Must match a URI registered on the integration.</p></div>
                <div class="doc-row"><code class="doc-path">PORT</code><span class="chip-method">Optional</span><p class="body-md doc-desc">Defaults to 3000.</p></div>
            </div>
            <pre class="doc-pre"># environment variables
GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=your_client_id
GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=your_client_secret

# optional — enables Notion connection
NOTION_CLIENT_ID=your_notion_client_id
NOTION_CLIENT_SECRET=your_notion_secret</pre>

            <h2 class="title-md">How sign-in works</h2>
            <ol class="steps-ol body-md">
                <li><strong>Authorize</strong> — /login redirects you to github.com with a random state value stored in a short-lived HttpOnly cookie.</li>
                <li><strong>Exchange</strong> — GitHub returns a one-time code; the server verifies state, then swaps code + client secret for an access token.</li>
                <li><strong>Session</strong> — a random session id cookie is issued; token, profile and repo data live server-side only. The browser never sees the token.</li>
            </ol>

            <h2 class="title-md">Routes</h2>
            <div class="doc-list">
                <div class="doc-row"><span class="chip-method">GET</span><code class="doc-path">/</code><p class="body-md doc-desc">Landing page when signed out; your access control panel once a session cookie is present.</p></div>
                <div class="doc-row"><span class="chip-method">GET</span><code class="doc-path">/docs</code><p class="body-md doc-desc">This page.</p></div>
                <div class="doc-row"><span class="chip-method">GET</span><code class="doc-path">/notion</code><p class="body-md doc-desc">Notion integration page — status, setup guide, and the shared-page panel.</p></div>
                <div class="doc-row"><span class="chip-method">GET</span><code class="doc-path">/login</code><p class="body-md doc-desc">Start GitHub OAuth (state cookie, 10 min).</p></div>
                <div class="doc-row"><span class="chip-method">ANY</span><code class="doc-path">/?code=&amp;state=</code><p class="body-md doc-desc">GitHub OAuth reply — accepted on the root path so whatever callback URL is registered works.</p></div>
                <div class="doc-row"><span class="chip-method">GET</span><code class="doc-path">/login/notion</code><p class="body-md doc-desc">Start Notion OAuth. Requires NOTION_CLIENT_ID / NOTION_CLIENT_SECRET and a registered redirect URI.</p></div>
                <div class="doc-row"><span class="chip-method">GET</span><code class="doc-path">/notion/callback</code><p class="body-md doc-desc">Notion OAuth reply. Verifies state, exchanges the code for an integration token, links the workspace to your session.</p></div>
                <div class="doc-row"><span class="chip-method">GET</span><code class="doc-path">/logout/notion</code><p class="body-md doc-desc">Unlinks the Notion workspace from your session (GitHub session untouched).</p></div>
                <div class="doc-row"><span class="chip-method">GET</span><code class="doc-path">/refresh</code><p class="body-md doc-desc">Re-fetches profile, repositories and organizations using the stored access token — no re-login required.</p></div>
                <div class="doc-row"><span class="chip-method">GET</span><code class="doc-path">/logout</code><p class="body-md doc-desc">Destroys the server-side session and clears the sid cookie.</p></div>
                <div class="doc-row"><span class="chip-method">GET</span><code class="doc-path">/about · /privacy · /terms</code><p class="body-md doc-desc">Legal &amp; about pages.</p></div>
                <div class="doc-row"><span class="chip-method">GET</span><code class="doc-path">/health</code><p class="body-md doc-desc">Health check: <code>{ ok, uptime }</code>.</p></div>
            </div>

            <h2 class="title-md">JSON API</h2>
            <div class="doc-list">
                <div class="doc-row"><span class="chip-method">GET</span><code class="doc-path">/api/access/:owner/:repo</code><p class="body-md doc-desc">Live JSON list of everyone with access to a repository — login, avatar URL, profile URL and role_name per person. Requires a session; returns { error: "unauthorized" } with 401 otherwise.</p></div>
                <div class="doc-row"><span class="chip-method">POST</span><code class="doc-path">/api/access/:owner/:repo</code><p class="body-md doc-desc">Invite a collaborator. JSON body: { user, permission } where user is a GitHub username or email address and permission is one of read | triage | write | maintain | admin.</p></div>
            </div>
            <pre class="doc-pre"># list everyone with access
curl http://localhost:3000/api/access/octocat/hello-world

# invite someone with write access
curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/access/octocat/hello-world \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"user":"teammate@company.com","permission":"write"}'</pre>

            <h2 class="title-md">OAuth scopes</h2>
            <div class="doc-list">
                <div class="doc-row"><code class="doc-path scope">read:user</code><p class="body-md doc-desc">Basic profile: name, avatar, follower counts, account age.</p></div>
                <div class="doc-row"><code class="doc-path scope">repo</code><p class="body-md doc-desc">Full read of public AND private repositories you can access, plus collaborator lists and invitations on repos you administer.</p></div>
                <div class="doc-row"><code class="doc-path scope">read:org</code><p class="body-md doc-desc">Organization memberships, so org sections can be listed with their recent repos.</p></div>
            </div>

            <h2 class="title-md">Project structure</h2>
            <pre class="doc-pre">OrbitAccess/
├── Program.cs        entry point & middleware pipeline
├── Models/           session, GitHub & Notion types
├── Services/         GitHub, Notion, stores, sessions
├── Controllers/      JSON API endpoints
├── Middleware/       security headers
├── Pages/            Razor Pages (routes + views)
└── wwwroot/          static assets + built React landing</pre>

            <h2 class="title-md">Security notes</h2>
            <ul class="steps-ol body-md">
                <li>Access tokens and all GitHub data stay in server memory / the JSON data store — never in the browser. The Notion connection token is the one exception: it is cached on local disk so reconnects aren't needed after a restart.</li>
                <li>The OAuth state parameter is verified on every callback (CSRF protection).</li>
                <li>All dynamic output is HTML-escaped; the JSON API path segments are URL-encoded before hitting GitHub.</li>
                <li>Security headers (CSP, X-Frame-Options, HSTS) are applied by middleware on every response.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="body-md caption-note">Questions? Start at Program.cs.</p>
        </article>
    </div>
</section>